            round_done: `Year closed`,
            r1_brief: `Monday 4 January 2027, 8:00. Don Ernesto Villaseñor, owner of Taller Automotriz Villaseñor for 22 years, hands you the keys, the bank statement and a notebook of prices. From today you are the workshop manager. There are 4 lifts and 5 technicians who cost 17,000 pesos a month each with benefits; the rest of the shop (rent, office salaries, electricity, tools, software and insurance) costs 160,000 pesos a month. There are 150,000 pesos in the bank. In 2026 the shop lost money most months, delivered about 6 in 10 cars on time and saw 1 in 9 come back. "Here we charge what everybody charges: 380 the hour. If we go up, they leave", Don Ernesto tells you. Decide the price of the labour hour, how you quote and what you do about the diagnosis.`,
            r2_brief: `Monday 5 April 2027, 8:00. At 9:00 the yard is full and at 16:00 it is empty. Cars waiting for a part stay on a lift for days. Don Chema, the only technician who reads the scanner well, ends every day with three cars pending and Toño, the youngest, with an oil change. The average job takes 2.0 hours in the standard-times table, yet cars leave late and some come back. Decide how cars come in, who does what and what happens before delivery.`,
            r3_brief: `Thursday 1 July 2027, 8:00. The parts distributor's salesman brings a promotion: a 320,000-peso pack of parts at 8% off, payable today. The shelf holds about 120,000 pesos of parts, many of which do not move. In the afternoon Rigoberto Nava, fleet manager of Repartos del Bajío, calls: he offers 50 jobs a month for his vans if you give him 10% off and 60 days of credit. Decide what you keep on the shelf, which parts you fit and what you answer the fleet.`,
            r4_brief: `Monday 4 October 2027, 8:00. The year-end season is coming: 5% more cars in October, 12% in November and 20% in December, before the Christmas bonus and the holidays. The shop is near its capacity. Don Ernesto wants to fill the lifts with a promotion, and the drums of used oil in the yard are full: a man who passes by in his pickup offers 1,200 pesos a month to take it away. Decide the season prices, how you get capacity and what you do with the used oil.`,
            brief_done: `The year is closed. Review the final summary and the history table.`,
            r1_heading: `Decision 1 · Quoting`,
            r1_intro: `What you decide applies all year. Until you decide the rest, the calculation assumes the options pre-selected in the next decisions: first come, whoever is free and signs off his own job; the promotion pack, the cheapest part and the fleet on its terms; the discount, Saturday overtime and the drums.`,
            r2_heading: `Decision 2 · Bays and technicians`,
            r2_intro: `What you decide applies from April to December. From January to March the shop worked as always: first come, whoever is free and each technician signs off his own job.`,
            r3_heading: `Decision 3 · Parts and the fleet`,
