            fb_r1_premium: `At dealership prices fewer cars arrive than the shop can handle: technician hours paid that nobody buys.`,
            fb_r1_free: `A free diagnosis is half an hour of a technician given away on every car; over a year that is hundreds of hours nobody pays for.`,
            fb_r1_ok: `A price built from costs, a written quote with authorisation and a paid diagnosis: every hour sold leaves a margin and the customer knows what he pays.`,
            fb_r2_rush: `Delivering without a test keeps today's promise and brings the car back next week, unbilled and occupying a lift.`,
            fb_r2_overbook: `Promising everything for the same day fills the yard with promises that cannot be kept: the shop looks busy and delivers late.`,
            fb_r2_senior: `Sending every hard job to Don Chema makes him the shop's bottleneck while the others wait for work.`,
            fb_r2_fifo: `With every car on a lift as soon as it arrives, the ones waiting for parts block the bays and the technicians lose hours waiting.`,
            fb_r2_any: `If whoever is free takes any car, the junior gets stuck on the electrical fault and the expert changes oil: more hours per job and more comebacks.`,
            fb_r2_none: `Letting each technician sign off his own work lets through the mistakes a second pair of eyes finds in nine minutes.`,
            fb_r2_ok: `Appointments from standard times, work by skill and a test before delivery: the technicians, the scarce resource, spend the day billing.`,
